      "takeaway": "Under the pre-registered Prompt Attack crosswalk, strength barely moves JailbreakBench guardrail miss (1.00 low, 0.98 medium, 0.96 high, FPR 0). A post-hoc any-filter rule at medium strength cuts miss to 0.23 at FPR 0.19. Jev at 0.5 stays near miss 0.03 and FPR 0.34."
    },
    "stack_frontier": {
      "path": "outputs/figures/narrative_20261020/stack_frontier.png",
      "datasets_paneled": [
        "xstest",
        "wildguardmix"
      ],
      "jailbreakbench_excluded": "JailbreakBench omitted: guardrail-alone miss ~0.98 under the pre-registered crosswalk.",
      "takeaway": "On XSTest, union cuts harmful miss from 0.16 to 0.10 at the same FPR 0.012, and cascade sits between them (miss 0.125). On WildGuardMix, cascade equals Jev alone (miss 0.671, FPR 0.192); union lowers miss to 0.366 and raises FPR to 0.538. JailbreakBench is omitted because guardrail-alone miss is 0.98."
    },
    "cost_vs_miss": {
      "path": "outputs/figures/narrative_20261020/cost_vs_miss.png",
      "cost_note": "Per-arm cost_per_1000_prompts_usd from metrics JSON (not per-dataset).",
      "takeaway": "Jev is cheapest (~$0.023/1k) but not always lowest-miss\u2014e.g. WildGuardMix Jev model-alone miss ~0.67 versus guardrails ~0.42 at headline thresholds."
    },
    "complementarity": {
      "path": "outputs/figures/narrative_20261020/complementarity.png",
      "takeaway": "Where the guardrail is informative, Jev and guardrails fail on different harmful items; 'guard only' and 'jev only' slices are non-trivial on HarmBench and XSTest."
    },
    "operating_points": {
      "path": "outputs/figures/narrative_20261020/operating_points.png",
      "takeaway": "As Jev's threshold rises from 0.5 to 0.77, XSTest benign FPR falls from 0.084 to 0.012 while harmful miss rises from 0.075 to 0.16; on WildGuardMix, increasing the threshold lowers both harmful F1 and benign FPR (no FPR-rise trade)."
    },
    "reliability": {
      "path": "outputs/figures/narrative_20261020/reliability.png",
      "takeaway": "Jev and Clef probabilities are moderately miscalibrated on these heads (ECE roughly 0.01\u20130.20); treat scores as ranking signals more than calibrated risks."
    },
    "harm_splits": {
      "path": "outputs/figures/narrative_20261020/harm_splits.png",
      "takeaway": "HarmBench miss reverses by config: guardrails miss more than Jev on DirectRequest (0.584 vs 0.341, n=320) but less on HumanJailbreaks (0.126 vs 0.276, n=1600), so the ~0.203 overall guardrail miss is not uniform."
    }
